你认为那是因为帕姆当时感觉很勇敢，所以她试图在那一刻说出自己的真实感受吗？

1363
01:04:11.480 --> 01:04:19.280
And then she backs out when she sees Karen's face and also how much of this was scripted and how much of it was improvised.
然后当她看到凯伦的表情时又退缩了，而且这段戏有多少是照剧本演的，又有多少是即兴发挥的？

1364
01:04:20.520 --> 01:04:25.600
OK, so first of all, this scene plays out exactly as it was scripted.
好的，首先，这场戏完全是按照剧本演的。

1365
01:04:25.600 --> 01:04:31.320
And all of those like awkward jumps in dialogue were all scripted.
所有那些对话中尴尬的跳跃也都是剧本写好的。

1366
01:04:31.600 --> 01:04:34.320
I just think it is such a great piece of writing.
我只是觉得这是一段非常棒的剧本。

1367
01:04:34.320 --> 01:04:41.940
And I remember I felt being challenged as an actor to make all of those different turns that Pam has to make in the scene.
我记得作为演员，我感到很有挑战性，要表现出帕姆在那场戏中所有不同的情绪转折。

1368
01:04:41.940 --> 01:04:48.500
And so when she says, oh, yeah, that's because she heard the question.
所以当她说“噢，是啊”时，那是因为她听到了那个问题。

1369
01:04:48.500 --> 01:04:50.520
You don't have feelings for Jim.
“你对吉姆没有感觉了。”

1370
01:04:50.720 --> 01:04:50.860
Right.
对。

1371
01:04:51.120 --> 01:04:54.000
And she's like, oh, yeah, I don't have feelings.
然后她就像是，噢，是啊，我没有感觉了。

1372
01:04:54.200 --> 01:04:55.540
But that's not what Karen said.
但凯伦说的并不是这个。

1373
01:04:55.760 --> 01:04:58.660
Karen said, you do you still have feelings for Jim?
凯伦说的是，你还对吉姆有感觉吗？

1374
01:04:58.880 --> 01:05:00.040
And she's like, oh, yeah.
然后她就像是，噢，是啊。

1375
01:05:00.920 --> 01:05:03.840
But like Pam is just like she's not hearing everything.
但帕姆当时就是，她没有听清所有内容。

1376
01:05:03.840 --> 01:05:10.460
And she's just like her mind is being blown right now by the fact that Jim told Karen this.
她只是，她现在被吉姆告诉了凯伦这件事的事实给震惊到了。

1377
01:05:10.820 --> 01:05:10.940
Yeah.
是啊。

1378
01:05:10.940 --> 01:05:12.540
And you know what?
而且你知道吗？

1379
01:05:12.620 --> 01:05:14.560
Because now it's everything we were talking about.
因为现在这就是我们刚才谈论的一切。

1380
01:05:14.900 --> 01:05:16.580
It's not a secret anymore.
这不再是一个秘密了。

1381
01:05:16.800 --> 01:05:19.000
It's not Jim and Pam's secret anymore.
这不再是吉姆和帕姆的秘密了。

1382
01:05:19.320 --> 01:05:26.320
That I think tells Pam that he's taking this relationship with Karen seriously because he's willing to tell her the real truth.
我认为这告诉帕姆，他正在认真对待与凯伦的关系，因为他愿意告诉她真相。

1383
01:05:26.540 --> 01:05:31.380
And now I think Pam is just in like a deer in headlights kind of mode.
而现在我觉得帕姆就像是陷入了惊慌失措的状态。

1384
01:05:31.560 --> 01:05:32.740
Well, I thought it was fantastic.
嗯，我觉得这太棒了。

1385
01:05:32.740 --> 01:05:35.320
I thought you the two of you did such a great job with it.
我觉得你们两个演得太好了。

1386
01:05:35.440 --> 01:05:37.900
It was written so well and acted so well.
剧本写得好，演得也很好。

1387
01:05:37.900 --> 01:05:40.560
And, oh, it made me so uncomfortable.
而且，噢，这让我感到非常不自在。

1388
01:05:40.660 --> 01:05:42.300
So you guys know you did the right.
所以你们知道你们做对了。

1389
01:05:42.500 --> 01:05:43.600
You did your job.
你们完成了你们的工作。

1390
01:05:44.760 --> 01:05:46.760
Rashida and I had a lot of fun shooting that scene.
拉什达和我拍那场戏时玩得很开心。

1391
01:05:47.120 --> 01:05:47.380
All right.
好的。

1392
01:05:47.520 --> 01:05:54.040
Should we go back down to the warehouse where Kevin is leading all of the guys in a card game?
我们要回到仓库看看凯文带着大家玩纸牌游戏吗？

1393
01:05:54.040 --> 01:05:54.220
Yeah.
好啊。

1394
01:05:54.360 --> 01:05:59.740
He says it's a no limit deuce to seven low ball, which I think is the same one he did in Casino Night, right?
他说这是“无上限二七低牌”，我想这和他之前在“赌场之夜”玩的是同一种，对吧？

1395
01:06:00.860 --> 01:06:07.120
Yes, that is what he won in the World Series of Poker, he tells us, in Casino Night.
是的，他在“赌场之夜”里告诉我们，他就是靠这个赢得了世界扑克系列赛。

1396
01:06:07.320 --> 01:06:09.780
And then Michael shuffles the cards like a total idiot.
然后迈克尔像个彻头彻尾的白痴一样洗牌。

1397
01:06:11.080 --> 01:06:11.600
Yes.
没错。

1398
01:06:12.040 --> 01:06:12.460
Yes.
是啊。

1399
01:06:12.460 --> 01:06:19.940
We had a fan catch from Katie who said in this episode around 12 minutes, 46 seconds, Kevin's wearing glasses again.
我们收到了一位粉丝凯蒂的发现，她说在这一集的12分46秒左右，凯文又戴上了眼镜。

1400
01:06:20.200 --> 01:06:21.200
There he is.
他就在那儿。

1401
01:06:21.340 --> 01:06:24.460
He wears glasses when he plays poker, but not when he's working.
他打扑克时会戴眼镜，但工作时不戴。

1402
01:06:24.700 --> 01:06:26.920
Not as an accountant, just when he plays cards.
不是当会计的时候，只是打牌的时候。

1403
01:06:26.920 --> 01:06:29.600
And this is when Elizabeth enters.
这时伊丽莎白登场了。

1404
01:06:29.900 --> 01:06:31.500
She comes out of Daryl's office.
她从达里尔的办公室里走出来。

1405
01:06:31.500 --> 01:06:41.900
She has changed out of her sweatpants and sweatshirt, and she is now in a breakaway, sexy office attire.
她换下了运动裤和运动衫，现在穿的是一套性感、易撕的办公装。

1406
01:06:42.240 --> 01:06:45.600
We had a huge fan catch from Kristen Trogel.
我们收到了克里斯汀·特罗格尔发来的一个很棒的发现。

1407
01:06:45.780 --> 01:06:47.460
Kristen, what'd you catch?
克里斯汀，你发现了什么？

1408
01:06:47.820 --> 01:06:54.840
Pam's shirt in the dundies is the same shirt that Elizabeth the stripper rips off in Ben Franklin.
帕姆在“邓迪奖”颁奖礼上穿的那件衬衫，和脱衣舞娘伊丽莎白在“本·富兰克林”那集里撕掉的是同一件。

1409
01:06:54.840 --> 01:06:58.180
Oh my God, did they recycle one of your shirts?
天哪，他们是循环利用了你的衬衫吗？

1410
01:06:58.440 --> 01:07:01.980
Did wardrobe make it like a breakaway kind of blouse or something?
是服装组把它改成了那种易撕的衬衫吗？

1411
01:07:03.180 --> 01:07:03.780
Yes.
是的。

1412
01:07:04.440 --> 01:07:05.040
Yes.
是的。

1413
01:07:05.300 --> 01:07:08.440
Elizabeth is wearing one of my old shirts.
伊丽莎白穿的是我的一件旧衬衫。

1414
01:07:08.940 --> 01:07:12.220
So I actually first wore it for basketball.
我其实最先是在打篮球时穿的它。

1415
01:07:12.820 --> 01:07:19.400
And then I wear it again in dundies, and I reached out to Carrie Bennett, our wardrobe supervisor, about this.
后来我在“邓迪奖”那集又穿了一次，我为此联系了我们的服装主管嘉莉·贝内特。

1416
01:07:19.560 --> 01:07:20.020
What'd she say?
她怎么说？

1417
01:07:21.260 --> 01:07:24.140
She said that this was not in the script.
她说剧本里并没有这一出。

1418
01:07:24.320 --> 01:07:27.640
This was not like any kind of direction she was given.
这并不是她收到的任何指示。

1419
01:07:27.860 --> 01:07:31.780
Because a lot of people did write in and ask, like, was this on purpose?
因为很多人写信来问，这是故意的吗？

1420
01:07:31.780 --> 01:07:37.540
Did you want us to notice that this was the identical shirt that Pam has worn?
你们是想让我们注意到这和帕姆穿的是同一件衬衫吗？

1421
01:07:37.540 --> 01:07:39.680
Was that a joke that was written in the script?
这是剧本里写的一个笑话吗？

1422
01:07:39.860 --> 01:07:40.720
It wasn't.
并不是。

1423
01:07:40.720 --> 01:07:49.180
She said that oftentimes when a guest actor is cast at the very last minute, she doesn't have time to go shopping for them.
她说通常当客串演员在最后一刻才定下来时，她没有时间去为他们购物。

1424
01:07:49.320 --> 01:07:55.320
So what wardrobe designers do is they go into their, quote unquote, retired wardrobe.
所以服装设计师的做法是去翻他们的“退役”服装库。

1425
01:07:55.800 --> 01:08:03.260
And this is a stash of outfits that have been retired, but that used to belong to the main cast members.
这是一堆已经不再使用，但曾经属于主要演员的服装。

1426
01:08:04.420 --> 01:08:10.400
So she had to find a shirt that fit Elizabeth, and then it had to be converted into a ripaway shirt.
所以她得找一件适合伊丽莎白的衬衫，然后还得把它改成易撕款。

1427
01:08:11.000 --> 01:08:23.000
And so they just didn't have time to go shopping and convert a shirt into a ripaway shirt because the timing of when Jackie was cast, they had to just go into Pam's old wardrobe.
因为杰基定角的时间太紧，他们没时间去买新衣服再改成易撕款，所以只能去翻帕姆的旧衣服。

1428
01:08:23.000 --> 01:08:24.060
And that's what they did.
他们就是这么做的。

1429
01:08:24.060 --> 01:08:26.160
And she said she can't believe that people noticed.
她说她真不敢相信居然有人注意到了。

1430
01:08:26.160 --> 01:08:33.020
Well, listen, Elizabeth, the stripper, you're lucky you didn't get any of Angela Martin's retired wardrobe.
听着，伊丽莎白，你该庆幸你没穿到安吉拉·马丁的退役服装。

1431
01:08:33.800 --> 01:08:34.620
Oh, no.
噢，不。

1432
01:08:35.420 --> 01:08:36.280
Oh, no.
噢，不。

1433
01:08:36.620 --> 01:08:37.900
That would have been very bad.
那可就太糟糕了。

1434
01:08:38.240 --> 01:08:38.840
That would have been very bad.
那可就太糟糕了。

1435
01:08:38.840 --> 01:08:39.980
That's a great catch, though.
不过这真是个了不起的发现。

1436
01:08:40.780 --> 01:08:41.660
I know.
我知道。

1437
01:08:41.820 --> 01:08:45.380
And Carrie also said that this happens all the time on TV shows.
嘉莉还说这种事在电视剧里经常发生。

1438
01:08:45.940 --> 01:08:51.320
She said you will often spot retired clothing from the main cast being repurposed for guest actors.
她说你经常会发现主要演员的退役服装被重新利用在客串演员身上。

1439
01:08:51.320 --> 01:08:56.400
I feel like everybody, you can look for that, along with the fakie bag.
我觉得大家以后可以留意一下，还有那个假包。

1440
01:08:56.460 --> 01:08:57.140
Fakie bag.
假包。

1441
01:08:57.300 --> 01:08:59.460
Well, now she starts her dance.
好了，现在她开始跳舞了。

1442
01:08:59.940 --> 01:09:01.440
It's to bad companies.
配乐是《Bad Company》。

1443
01:09:01.760 --> 01:09:02.780
Feel like making love.
还有《Feel Like Makin' Love》。

1444
01:09:04.000 --> 01:09:05.960
No one wanted the dance.
没人想要这段舞蹈。

1445
01:09:06.140 --> 01:09:07.200
Bob Vance didn't want it.
鲍勃·万斯也不想要。

1446
01:09:07.320 --> 01:09:08.260
Michael's like, okay.
迈克尔心想，好吧。

1447
01:09:09.200 --> 01:09:11.600
And this is so awkward.
这真是太尴尬了。

1448
01:09:11.920 --> 01:09:13.560
He doesn't know what to do with himself.
他不知道该怎么办才好。

1449
01:09:13.560 --> 01:09:14.420
He's so uncomfortable.
他感到非常不自在。

1450
01:09:14.760 --> 01:09:17.120
He just starts muttering, you smell like Tide.
他只是开始嘟囔着说，你闻起来像汰渍洗衣液。

1451
01:09:17.580 --> 01:09:18.480
Yep, smell like Tide.
没错，闻起来像汰渍。

1452
01:09:18.560 --> 01:09:19.240
Do you use Tide?
你用汰渍吗？

1453
01:09:19.240 --> 01:09:21.240
We had a couple of people write in.
我们收到了一些观众来信。

1454
01:09:21.500 --> 01:09:27.780
Zuyi and Dan asked, when Elizabeth is dancing on Michael, how much of the dialogue was scripted?
Zuyi和Dan问，当Elizabeth在Michael身上跳舞时，有多少对话是写在剧本里的？

1455
01:09:28.520 --> 01:09:29.320
All of it.
全部都是。

1456
01:09:29.480 --> 01:09:36.220
And, you guys, we've talked a little bit about, like, scenes where someone has to slap someone, you know?
而且，伙计们，我们之前聊过一些关于比如有人需要扇别人耳光的场景，你们懂的？

1457
01:09:36.420 --> 01:09:38.980
And how we bring in a stunt coordinator.
以及我们是如何引入特技指导的。

1458
01:09:39.420 --> 01:09:41.760
You do that kind of stuff in scenes like this, too.
像这样的场景，你们也会做同样的处理。

1459
01:09:41.760 --> 01:09:50.100
Any scenes that have any kind of, like, touching, dancing up on someone, a sex scene, they are choreographed.
任何涉及某种接触、贴身热舞、性爱场面的戏，都是编排好的。

1460
01:09:50.120 --> 01:09:50.320
A fight scene.
打斗戏也是。

1461
01:09:50.740 --> 01:09:50.960
You do not freak.
你不会感到惊慌。

1462
01:09:50.960 --> 01:09:53.080
Yeah, it's really no different than, like, a fight scene.
是的，这和打斗戏真的没什么区别。

1463
01:09:53.140 --> 01:09:54.140
It's like, I'm going to sit here.
就像是，我要坐在这儿。

1464
01:09:54.220 --> 01:09:55.300
I'm going to put my arm here.
我要把胳膊放在这儿。

1465
01:09:55.540 --> 01:09:57.020
Then I'm going to stand here.
然后我要站在这儿。

1466
01:09:57.520 --> 01:09:58.520
It's all rehearsed.
这一切都是排练好的。

1467
01:09:58.520 --> 01:10:00.140
You don't freestyle this stuff.
这种戏不能即兴发挥。

1468
01:10:00.520 --> 01:10:00.960
Yeah.
没错。

1469
01:10:00.960 --> 01:10:08.620
Yeah, so where she sits on his leg, all of the dancing she's going to do, when she's going to rip open her shirt, very scripted.
是的，所以她坐在他腿上的位置，她要跳的所有舞步，她什么时候撕开衬衫，都是严格按照剧本来的。

1470
01:10:08.840 --> 01:10:10.140
The dialogue was scripted.
对话也是写在剧本里的。

1471
01:10:10.300 --> 01:10:18.680
I wasn't surprised when I went back to the script because I thought, yeah, I don't think in a moment like this that they would have, like, freestyled that.
当我回头看剧本时我并不惊讶，因为我想，没错，我觉得在这种时刻他们不可能即兴发挥。

1472
01:10:18.680 --> 01:10:20.260
No, that was all scripted.
不，那全是剧本写好的。

1473
01:10:20.580 --> 01:10:23.560
And Michael is just overwhelmed.
而Michael当时不知所措。

1474
01:10:23.560 --> 01:10:24.700
He's like, this is wrong.
他心想，这不对劲。

1475
01:10:24.700 --> 01:10:25.500
I have a girlfriend.
我有女朋友。

1476
01:10:25.500 --> 01:10:27.480
And he storms off.
然后他气冲冲地走了。

1477
01:10:27.660 --> 01:10:29.280
It was just all too much for him.
这一切对他来说实在太难以承受了。

1478
01:10:29.680 --> 01:10:35.580
And Dwight, being the frugal fella he is, is like, hey, I paid you for three hours.
而Dwight，作为一个节俭的家伙，心想，嘿，我付了你三个小时的钱。

1479
01:10:36.320 --> 01:10:38.000
I'm going to get three hours of work out of you.
我就要让你干满三个小时的活。

1480
01:10:38.120 --> 01:10:39.620
So now you have to go answer phones.
所以现在你得去接电话。

1481
01:10:39.920 --> 01:10:45.120
And because Oscar is nowhere to be seen, even though he has returned.
而且因为Oscar不见踪影，尽管他已经回来了。

1482
01:10:45.420 --> 01:10:47.520
Did we shoot this out of order, Jenna?
Jenna，我们是乱序拍摄的吗？

1483
01:10:47.520 --> 01:10:48.980
Why isn't Oscar there?
为什么Oscar不在那儿？

1484
01:10:49.340 --> 01:10:53.520
I don't know, because the traveling salesman and the return were shot in October.
我不知道，因为《旅行推销员》和《回归》是在十月份拍摄的。

1485
01:10:53.760 --> 01:10:54.080
Yeah.
是的。

1486
01:10:54.440 --> 01:10:55.720
And this was shot in January.
而这一集是在一月份拍的。

1487
01:10:56.200 --> 01:10:59.320
So it doesn't make sense why Oscar isn't there.
所以Oscar不在那儿确实说不通。

1488
01:10:59.520 --> 01:10:59.720
It doesn't.
确实说不通。

1489
01:10:59.880 --> 01:11:04.500
So anyway, Dwight brings Elizabeth to accounting to sit in Oscar's seat.
总之，Dwight把Elizabeth带到会计部，让她坐在Oscar的位子上。

1490
01:11:04.820 --> 01:11:07.240
Elizabeth is very overwhelming for Angela.
Elizabeth对Angela来说太有压迫感了。

1491
01:11:07.440 --> 01:11:13.560
And she's like, like, sort of like this very Elizabethan, like, fanning myself.
她当时就像是，那种非常伊丽莎白时代的，不停地给自己扇风。

1492
01:11:14.320 --> 01:11:15.780
Well, here's the thing.
好吧，重点是。

1493
01:11:15.780 --> 01:11:18.220
She compliments your baby poster.
她夸奖了你的婴儿海报。

1494
01:11:18.980 --> 01:11:20.100
It doesn't matter.
那不重要。

1495
01:11:20.300 --> 01:11:21.160
It doesn't matter.
那不重要。

1496
01:11:21.280 --> 01:11:21.660
I know.
我知道。

1497
01:11:21.860 --> 01:11:23.080
She really is.
她确实是。

1498
01:11:23.180 --> 01:11:26.220
She's a fan of baby jazz, like your character is.
她和你饰演的角色一样，是爵士乐宝宝的粉丝。

1499
01:11:26.740 --> 01:11:28.620
But a lot of people wrote in.
不过很多人来信问。

1500
01:11:29.320 --> 01:11:34.760
Sierra, Tiffany, Camille, and Krista are like, what is the baby poster doing back up?
Sierra、Tiffany、Camille和Krista问，那张婴儿海报怎么又挂回去了？

1501
01:11:36.320 --> 01:11:40.200
Angela, did your character put it up when Oscar went on his sabbatical?
安吉拉，奥斯卡休假的时候，你的角色是不是把海报又贴回去了？

1502
01:11:40.360 --> 01:11:41.420
That's what they want to know.
大家想知道的就是这个。

1503
01:11:41.600 --> 01:11:42.620
I love this theory.
我喜欢这个理论。

1504
01:11:42.620 --> 01:11:44.020
I fully support it.
